 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "G-20",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "location": "CONTRACT.md section 7 'Environment predicate (S10)', MC30, MC31; CONTRACT.json environment.os_supplied_allowance, controls",
   "summary": "For any one process, only one of MC30's two branches (with or without the variable) can be produced for real; the other must be labelled a simulated boundary. MC31 has no Node start, so the probe's own refusal of a wrong recorded value or an extra variable is never run in a real probe. 'If the process has loaded CoreFoundation' reads as a check that the JSON predicate does not contain."
  },
  {
   "id": "G-21",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "location": "CONTRACT.md section 4 'Identity bound by M0' and 'Python-side Mach-O rules', MC32; CONTRACT.json python.bound_by_m0, python.mach_o_rules",
   "summary": "Four precisions are missing: (1) exact-set comparison of the trees: 1,390 of 1,804 standard-library modules lack bytecode and the tree is owner-writable, yet MC32 tests only changed files, not added ones; (2) transitive dependencies, and the symbolic-link hops of their referenced paths (every dependency is reached via <prefix>/opt links, and libssl reaches libcrypto by a second path); (3) the interpreter-selection chain (the venv link and pyvenv.cfg home) outside both trees; (4) that @-relative LC_RPATH entries such as libmpdec's @loader_path/../lib are recorded search directories, not references that must resolve to a bound file."
  },
  {
   "id": "G-22",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "location": "READ-SET.json host_facts (revision 3 entry); CONTRACT.md section 1 'Document schemas'; CONTRACT.json schemas",
   "summary": "The new host fact lists four variables for a five-variable launch (UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE missing). The preparer's install and install-result schemas and M0's plan schema are not in the versioned set, although their meaning changes under 0.2.0."
  }
 ],
